Practical NO: 1

Aim :- 

Introduction to Linux and Terminal Basics:
Understand Basic Linux environment and command-line usage.

Theory:-

Linux is an open-source operating system widely used for servers, programming, networking, and cybersecurity. The Terminal is a command line interface used to interact with the Linux system using commands.

Requirements:

•Linux Operating system
•Terminal
•Basic knowledge of Linux commands.

Command explanation :-

a) Open terminal and execute basic commands.

$ whoami :- Display the username of the currently logged-in-user.

$ date :- Display the current system date and time

$ cal :- Display the calendar of the current month.

$ uname :- Display basic information about the Linux operating system.

b) Display current directory using

$ pwd :- Display the full path of the current working directory.

c) View logged-in users using

$ who :- Display the users currently logged into the system.

d) Clear screen and exit terminal

$ clear :- Clears all previous output from the terminal screen

$ exit :- closes the current terminal session.

